  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Par 210.04 Order of Proceeding, Testimony.\n\n(a) Any person offering testimony, evidence or arguments shall state his/her name on the record. If the person is representing another person, the person being represented shall also be identified by name.\n\n(b) Testimony shall be offered in the following order:\n\n(1) The probation/parole officer and such witnesses as the officer may call; and\n\n(2) The parolee opposing the probation/parole officer, and such witnesses as the parolee or his attorney may call.\n\nSource. #7149, eff 12-7-99, EXPIRED: 12-7-07\n\nNew. #9070, INTERIM, eff 1-11-08, EXPIRED: 7-9-08\n\nNew. #9254, eff 9-6-08; ss by #12157, eff 4-7-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/par100-500.html"
